  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.3.0: depends on Jakar.Core. Gains TelemetrySource, TelemetrySpan, AppVersion (+ flags), AppInformation, DeviceInformation (+ category/platform/types), GcInfo/GcMemoryInformation/GcGenerationInformation, StopWatch, SelfLogger, FuzzyEqualizer, ExceptionDetails/MethodDetails/ParameterDetails (from Jakar.Extensions, which type-forwards them), and everything that was in Jakar.Logging.Serilog: LogEventProperties, DeviceInformationEnricher, TelemetrySourceEnricher, OpenTelemetryActivityEnricher, AppLoggerOptions.CreateLogger(TelemetrySource)/Info. ThreadInformation stays in Jakar.Extensions; its Serilog property is RuntimeProperties.Thread(). Use with Jakar.Extensions 10.13.0 or later. 10.2.0: BREAKING: no longer depends on Jakar.Extensions or Jakar.Files (Serilog, Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions/Options and System.IO.Hashing only). The Jakar.Extensions parts moved to the new Jakar.Logging.Serilog: LogEventProperties (AppInformation/ThreadInformation/GcInfo/DeviceInformation properties), DeviceInformationEnricher, OpenTelemetryActivityEnricher (app and device properties from a TelemetrySource) and AppLoggerOptions.CreateLogger(TelemetrySource). Here: ActivityEnricher (spans, plus thread and GC state from RuntimeProperties on warnings) replaces OpenTelemetryActivityEnricher; IOpenTelemetryActivityEnricher is gone. AppLoggerOptions is no longer a BaseClass or disposable, has no DeviceInfo/Info, uses string paths (AppDataDirectory, CacheDirectory, LogsDirectory, SeqBuffer, LogsFile, ScreenshotFile) instead of LocalDirectory/FilePaths, CreateLogger(Action<LoggerConfiguration>?) replaces CreateLogger(TelemetrySource), and ConfigureLogger no longer takes a TelemetrySource; the folder/template constants are on AppLoggerOptions. ScreenShot.File is a path. Enricher lost its AppVersion/GcGenerationInformation overloads. 10.1.0: initial release. Split out of Jakar.Extensions 10.12.0; the types keep the Jakar.Extensions namespace.",
